/* book Worked example 2: Q: In a combined test on the same 10 bar main, the separator collects 0.5 kg of water while 9.5 kg of steam passes on to the throttling part, which gives the outlet state of the first example (1 bar, 130 °C). Find the dryness fraction of the main steam.
   1. Separator: xs = ms/(ms + mw) = 9.5/(9.5 + 0.5) = 0.95.
   2. Throttling part: xt = 0.980, as in the first example.
   3. Vapour in the sample: xt × ms = 0.980 × 9.5 = 9.31 kg, out of a total of 9.5 + 0.5 = 10 kg.
   4. x = 9.31/10 = 0.931, which is the same as xs × xt = 0.95 × 0.980.
   Answer: The main steam has x ≈ 0.931, too wet for the throttling calorimeter alone (limit 0.949 at 10 bar). */
